# Root build context, used by services that need something outside their
# own directory copied into their image: services/gateway/ needs
# contracts/, spike-backbone and matrix-circle-service need
# backbone/interfaces.py. Docker only reads a .dockerignore from the
# *context root*, so this file is what applies to those builds -- the
# per-service ones they used to have are gone, since they'd have looked
# active while being silently ignored.
#
# ai-services still builds from its own directory as its context, so
# ai-services/.dockerignore is still the live file for that one.

.git/
.env

# Virtualenvs -- a committed venv can be tens of MB of build context
**/venv/
**/.venv/

**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache/

# Test-only material: images ship runtime code, tests run on the host
# (see README.md -- .dockerignore excluding tests/ is exactly why the
# "run tests in the container" instruction was wrong).
**/tests/
**/conftest.py
**/requirements-dev.txt

# Not part of any service image
docs/
clients/
infra/
db/
*.zip
